# React and TypeScript

## Stack conventions

- React 19 functional components with explicit prop types
- Do not use `React.FC`
- Avoid `any` unless justified in a comment
- No `enum` — TypeScript `erasableSyntaxOnly` requires const maps / union types
- Path alias: `@/` → `src/`

## Patterns in this project

- Lift Tiptap `useEditor` to the page (e.g. `EditorPage`); pass `editor` into presentational components
- Use `immediatelyRender: false` with Tiptap + React 19
- Normalize stored editor JSON with `normalizeTiptapContent` / `EMPTY_TIPTAP_DOC` before `setContent`
- Handle loading, error, empty, and success UI where data is fetched
- Preserve existing behavior when editing components

## After changes

- Prefer existing hooks and utilities over new abstractions
- Verify types via `npm run build` (`tsc -b && vite build`) and run `npm test` when logic changes
